abstract: This metadata package contains samples collected as part of a three-year
  initiative aimed at identifying and filling gaps in DNA barcode sequence availability
  for coastal marine micro-invertebrates. We used year-round, bi-weekly collections
  at a fixed near-shore location in Hyacinth Bay near Quadra Island British Columbia
  to survey the seasonal diversity of zooplankton and other micro-invertebrates. Additional
  samples were collected from a broader range of depths and habitats in the surrounding
  region using plankton nets, light traps, and short-term recruitment devices (settlement
  plates). DNA barcoding targeting the mitochondrial COI gene was successful for 2,914
  specimens spanning 15 different phyla.
